# Build artifacts
*.phar
# NOTE: composer.lock is deliberately NOT ignored here — this repo commits
# it by S440 law (tracked since 8e60cfc; the audit gate is built on the
# pinned lock: tests/SecurityAuditCheckTest.php's testTheCommittedLockExists
# asserts the file and parses it for the whole-lock audit). The pre-S440
# scaffold carried an ignore line for it — the known family contradiction:
# it makes a regenerated lock invisible to staging and would let a PR
# silently drop the lock where the `composer-audit` leg (--locked, no
# install step by design) then fails confusingly. Kept out on purpose, not
# an oversight.

# Testing
.phpunit.result.cache
coverage/

# Code style
.phpcs.cache/
